\f4\fs26 As the hover-copt took off, the three giant fans flailed about madly in effort to remain stable and in the air. These triple-blade egg-beaters had sophisticated computer assisted flight systems, without which the vessel would plummet to the ground in double quick time \'96 assuming of course that you could get it airborne in the first place. Just like helicopters of old, these craft were actively trying to crash every airborne microsecond \'96 even with computer assistance, flying these suckers was still a bit hit and miss. \
\'93Where to?\'94 Asked the pilot. \'93Shakti said anywhere you want to go.\'94 \
\'93Still up for that drink?\'94 Sarah said quietly to Cracker. \'93We cannot let this guy know where we live.\'94\
Cracker turned to the pilot and with the best upper crust accent he could muster requested, \'93To \'91The Quarter\'92 driver and don\'92t spare the horses.\'94 He knew it wasn\'92t funny, but found he could not stop himself. 
\f5\i Why do I say these things?
\f4\i0 \
\'93The Quarter? Are you guys feeling okay?\'94 asked the pilot incredulously. \'93That place is crime central.\'94\
\'93Yes, we are certain. The Quarter. Where the Elvi live.\'94 Cracker reiterated.\
 \'93The Elvi?\'94 Sarah was most confused.\
\'93Not Elvy, ELV-EYE. The plural of Elvis.\'94 He just got a blank stare. \'93Never heard of the Elvi? Jesus Christ, where have you been?\'94\
\'93Enjoying the fruits of social inequality, of course. What do you think? I have only been at street level a few times before and never after a terrorist attack. I have no idea what you people get up to.\'94 Sarah said as a \'91matter-of-factly\'92 as she could. \
\'93What \'91you people\'92 get up to? Well, Lady Posenby, we die. We die horribly. We work, so you can play and we suffer for your amusement. When we are not doing that, we get drunk and listen to music.\'94 \
\'93Music?\'94 She said, deliberately ignoring Cracker\'92s pain-and-suffering diatribe. \'93Music. That is something we have in common then.\'94\
\'93If you like old time, you are in for a treat. The Elvi are the best, they can do any old song and their voices are amazing, just amazing.\'94 He said, deciding to leave the social inequality debate for another day.\
\'93Who are these Elvi?\'94 She asked, having never heard of them.\
